INT. POTTERY KILN SHED - DUSK

Brick walls. A squat kiln glowing orange at its seams. Shelves of unglazed bowls. Clay dust in the air like flour.

LEILANI KAHALE (30s, apron, forearms grey with slip) crouches at the kiln, peering through a peephole. DARIUS PELLEGRINO-OKAFOR (30s, jacket, an umbrella he does not need) stands in the doorway holding a paper bag.

LEILANI
You're letting the heat out.

DARIUS
Sorry.

He steps in. Closes the door.

DARIUS (CONT'D)
I brought dumplings.

LEILANI
I'm firing.

DARIUS
I can wait.

LEILANI
It's six hours.

DARIUS
Then I brought a lot of dumplings.

She almost smiles. Turns back to the peephole.

LEILANI
Cone eight is down. Cone nine soon.

DARIUS
Is that good?

LEILANI
It's necessary.

He sets the bag on a shelf. Wanders along the bowls, touching the rims with one finger. She watches him, in profile, across the glow of the kiln.

DARIUS
These are beautiful.

LEILANI
They're unfinished.

DARIUS
So am I.

LEILANI
That's a terrible line.

DARIUS
I know. I rehearsed it.

She laughs. He turns. Their eyes meet.

LEILANI
I missed you.
DARIUS
^I missed you.

Both stop. The kiln ticks. Neither moves.

LEILANI
Stay.

DARIUS
For the firing?

LEILANI
For the firing.

He crosses the shed, sits on an upturned bucket by the kiln, and opens the bag. Steam rises, ginger and sesame. She sits beside him on the floor. He passes her a dumpling. She holds it up to the orange light.

LEILANI (CONT'D)
Six hours.

DARIUS
We have time.
